{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent positive bias: the model is generally too high versus realized prices, especially in downtrends. Apply a downward level shift (larger at longer horizons).",
    "Trend/lag error: during selloffs the model underestimates the speed and depth of declines (forecasts revert upward too early). Increase downside momentum / reduce mean-reversion strength when the last 10–20 days are falling.",
    "Horizon-dependent overshoot: errors widen with horizon (roughly days 10–25), where forecasts drift back up while outcomes stay lower. Use a horizon-increasing negative correction (e.g., small for days 1–5, larger for days 10–30).",
    "Post-drop rebound overprediction: after sharp down moves, the model predicts rebounds that are too strong and too soon. Cap rebound amplitude and delay rebound timing by several days after large negative returns.",
    "Local peaks too sticky: when recent history shows a lower-high / rolling decline, the model still prints mid-70s even as outcomes settle mid-60s. Add regime filter: if 20–30d slope is negative, compress forecast range downward and reduce volatility of upward swings."
  ]
}
